# Security Policy

## Reporting a Vulnerability

If you find a security vulnerability in {{ project_name }}, please report it through [GitHub's private vulnerability reporting](https://github.com/{{ github_org }}/{{ project_slug }}/security/advisories/new). This keeps the details private while we work on a fix.

Please include:

- What you found and how to reproduce it
- Which version you're using
- Any relevant logs or output (redact secrets)

## Security Measures

This project ships with security hardening out of the box:

- **All GitHub Actions pinned by SHA** with version comments, not floating tags. Dependabot opens PRs for updates.
- **Minimal workflow permissions** (`permissions: {}` at the top level, scoped per job).
- **`persist-credentials: false`** on checkout steps to prevent token leakage.
- **Concurrency groups** to cancel redundant workflow runs.
- **Secret scanning** via [gitleaks](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks) in pre-commit hooks.
- **Dependency updates** via [Dependabot](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/dependabot) on a weekly schedule.
- **PyPI publishing** uses Trusted Publishers with OIDC and Sigstore build provenance attestation (when enabled).

## Response Times

This is a volunteer-maintained open source project. Security reports are taken seriously, but there are no guaranteed response times.

## Supported Versions

Security fixes are applied to the latest release on the `main` branch. There is no backport policy for older versions.
